searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"BotArmy.Pulse","doc":"Pulse publishing module.\n\nThe pulse is a bot's current state and activity. It's published periodically\nto `bot.army.pulse. ` and provides real-time visibility into what\neach bot is doing.","ref":"BotArmy.Pulse.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Pulse Schema - BotArmy.Pulse","doc":"```json\n{\n  \"bot_id\": \"gtd_bot\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-21T10:30:00Z\",\n  \"status\": \"active|idle|busy|error\",\n  \"current_task\": \"processing_inbox\",\n  \"task_count\": 14,\n  \"queue_depth\": 5,\n  \"last_action\": \"task_created\",\n  \"uptime_seconds\": 86400,\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"llm_calls_today\": 23,\n    \"tasks_processed\": 142,\n    \"errors_today\": 0\n  }\n}\n```","ref":"BotArmy.Pulse.html#module-pulse-schema"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage - BotArmy.Pulse","doc":"```elixir\n# Publish a pulse for the current bot\nBotArmy.Pulse.publish(:gtd_bot, %{\n  status: :active,\n  current_task: \"processing_inbox\",\n  task_count: 14\n})\n```","ref":"BotArmy.Pulse.html#module-usage"},{"type":"module","title":"Subscribers - BotArmy.Pulse","doc":"The Context Broker subscribes to all `bot.army.pulse.*` subjects to:\n- Build a real-time \"army state\" dashboard\n- Detect stale bots (no pulse in 60s = potential issue)\n- Coordinate cross-bot activities\n\nAlerting on stale pulses is handled by `army.health.check` subscriber.","ref":"BotArmy.Pulse.html#module-subscribers"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmy.Pulse.build_state/2","doc":"Build a pulse state from bot metadata.\n\nConvenience function for bots to publish their current state.","ref":"BotArmy.Pulse.html#build_state/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmy.Pulse.publish/3","doc":"Publish a pulse for a bot.\n\nPublishes to `bot.army.pulse. ` with the provided state.","ref":"BotArmy.Pulse.html#publish/3"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmy.Soul","doc":"Soul storage and retrieval module.\n\nThe soul is the personality identity of a bot - its character voice, tone,\npriorities, and refusal rules. Stored as JSONB in PostgreSQL.","ref":"BotArmy.Soul.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Soul Schema - BotArmy.Soul","doc":"```json\n{\n  \"identity\": {\n    \"name\": \"GTD Bot\",\n    \"symbol\": \"◉\",\n    \"role\": \"Surface the next right action\"\n  },\n  \"tone\": \"conversational\",\n  \"verbosity\": \"medium\",\n  \"priorities\": [\"actionability\", \"clarity\", \"warmth\"],\n  \"refusals\": [\"judgmental\", \"saccharine\", \"overly technical\"],\n  \"failure_behavior\": \"honest but kind\"\n}\n```","ref":"BotArmy.Soul.html#module-soul-schema"},{"type":"module","title":"Storage - BotArmy.Soul","doc":"Soul configs are stored in PostgreSQL using the `souls` table:\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE souls (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY,\n  bot_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  tenant_id UUID NOT NULL,\n  config JSONB NOT NULL,\n  version INTEGER DEFAULT 1,\n  active BOOLEAN DEFAULT true,\n  inserted_at TIMESTAMPTZ,\n  updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ\n);\n```","ref":"BotArmy.Soul.html#module-storage"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage - BotArmy.Soul","doc":"```elixir\n# Get the current soul for a bot\nsoul = BotArmy.Soul.get(:gtd_bot)\n\n# Get soul for a specific tenant\nsoul = BotArmy.Soul.get(:gtd_bot, tenant_id: \"uuid-here\")\n\n# Update soul config\n{:ok, _} = BotArmy.Soul.update(:gtd_bot, %{tone: \"more sarcastic\"})\n```","ref":"BotArmy.Soul.html#module-usage"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmy.Soul.changeset/2","doc":"Returns a changeset for soul creation/update.","ref":"BotArmy.Soul.html#changeset/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmy.Soul.get/2","doc":"Get the current soul for a bot.\n\nReturns the active soul with the highest version for the given bot and tenant.","ref":"BotArmy.Soul.html#get/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmy.Soul.get/2","doc":"iex> BotArmy.Soul.get(:gtd_bot)\n    %BotArmy.Soul{config: %{\"identity\" => %{...}}}\n\n    iex> BotArmy.Soul.get(:gtd_bot, tenant_id: \"uuid\")\n    %BotArmy.Soul{config: %{\"identity\" => %{...}}}","ref":"BotArmy.Soul.html#get/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmy.Soul.publish/2","doc":"Publish soul to NATS for the given bot.\n\nPublishes to `bot.army.soul. ` with the current soul config.","ref":"BotArmy.Soul.html#publish/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmy.Soul.upsert/3","doc":"Create or update a soul configuration.\n\nUses INSERT ... ON CONFLICT to handle upserts.","ref":"BotArmy.Soul.html#upsert/3"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime","doc":"BotArmyRuntime provides the shared persistence and messaging foundation for the Bot Army ecosystem.\n\nThis module serves as the entry point for:\n\n- **Ecto Persistence**: A base `Repo` module that all Bot Army services inherit from for database access\n- **NATS Integration**: Connection management and publishing utilities for the Bot Army messaging bus\n- **Telemetry**: Structured logging and metrics collection across all services\n- **Supervision**: Application supervision tree setup","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Core Components - BotArmyRuntime","doc":"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.html#module-core-components"},{"type":"module","title":"Ecto Persistence (BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo) - BotArmyRuntime","doc":"Provides a shared database repository that:\n- Manages connections to PostgreSQL\n- Handles connection pooling and supervision\n- Supports migrations\n- Provides runtime configuration for all bot services","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.html#module-ecto-persistence-botarmyruntime-ecto-repo"},{"type":"module","title":"NATS Messaging (BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection and BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher) - BotArmyRuntime","doc":"Manages connections to the NATS message bus:\n- Maintains persistent connections with reconnection logic\n- Publishes messages to NATS subjects\n- Handles backpressure and connection errors","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.html#module-nats-messaging-botarmyruntime-nats-connection-and-botarmyruntime-nats-publisher"},{"type":"module","title":"Telemetry (BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry) - BotArmyRuntime","doc":"Provides structured observability:\n- Logging in JSON format\n- Metrics collection hooks\n- Performance monitoring","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.html#module-telemetry-botarmyruntime-telemetry"},{"type":"module","title":"Configuration - BotArmyRuntime","doc":"Configure in your application's `config.exs`:\n\n    config :bot_army_runtime, BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo,\n      database: \"bot_army_dev\",\n      username: \"postgres\",\n      password: \"postgres\",\n      hostname: \"localhost\",\n      pool_size: 10\n\n    config :bot_army_runtime, :nats,\n      servers: [{\"localhost\", 4222}],\n      ping_interval: 30_000","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage - BotArmyRuntime","doc":"Most applications will use this through the generated bot service schemas\n(e.g., `bot_army_schemas_gtd`). Direct usage is minimal:\n\n    # Publishing a message\n    {:ok, _} = BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.publish(\"subject\", %{\"event\" => \"data\"})\n\n    # Querying the database\n    result = BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.all(MySchema)","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.html#module-usage"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.version/0","doc":"Returns the version of bot_army_runtime.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.html#version/0"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Application","doc":"Supervision tree for BotArmyRuntime.\n\nStarts:\n- Registry for NATS connection status broadcasts\n- PromEx metrics collection\n- Cowboy HTTP endpoint for /metrics (port configurable via METRICS_PORT env, default 9090)\n- Telemetry handlers\n- NATS Connection (message bus connection)\n- NATS Dedup (message deduplication)","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Application.html"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo","doc":"Base Ecto Repository for Bot Army services.\n\nAll bot services inherit from this module to get database access. It handles:\n\n- Connection pooling and supervision\n- Runtime configuration\n- Migration support\n- Error handling","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Configuration - BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo","doc":"Configure in `config.exs`:\n\n    config :bot_army_runtime, BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo,\n      database: \"bot_army_dev\",\n      username: \"postgres\",\n      password: \"postgres\",\n      hostname: \"localhost\",\n      port: 5432,\n      pool_size: 10,\n      queue_target: 500,\n      queue_interval: 1000\n\nFor production, pass these via runtime configuration or environment variables:\n\n    config :bot_army_runtime, BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo,\n      database: {:system, \"DB_NAME\"},\n      username: {:system, \"DB_USER\"},\n      password: {:system, \"DB_PASSWORD\"},\n      hostname: {:system, \"DB_HOST\"},\n      pool_size: {:system, \"DB_POOL_SIZE\", \"10\"}","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage in Bot Services - BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo","doc":"A bot service would define:\n\n    defmodule BotArmyGTD.Repo do\n      use BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo\n    end\n\nThen configure:\n\n    config :bot_army_gtd, BotArmyGTD.Repo,\n      database: \"bot_army_gtd_dev\"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#module-usage-in-bot-services"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.aggregate/3","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.aggregate/3 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#aggregate/3"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.aggregate/4","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.aggregate/4 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#aggregate/4"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.all/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.all/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#all/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.all_by/3","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.all_by/3 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#all_by/3"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.checked_out?/0","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.checked_out?/0 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#checked_out?/0"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.checkout/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.checkout/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#checkout/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.child_spec/1","doc":"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.config/0","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.config/0 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#config/0"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.default_options/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.default_options/1 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#default_options/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.delete/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.delete/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#delete/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.delete!/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.delete!/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#delete!/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.delete_all/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.delete_all/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#delete_all/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.disconnect_all/2","doc":"Forces all connections in the repo pool to disconnect within the given interval.\n\nOnce this function is called, the pool will disconnect all of its connections\nas they are checked in or as they are pinged. Checked in connections will be\nrandomly disconnected within the given time interval. Pinged connections are\nimmediately disconnected - as they are idle (according to `:idle_interval`).\n\nIf the connection has a backoff configured (which is the case by default),\ndisconnecting means an attempt at a new connection will be done immediately\nafter, without starting a new process for each connection. However, if backoff\nhas been disabled, the connection process will terminate. In such cases,\ndisconnecting all connections may cause the pool supervisor to restart\ndepending on the max_restarts/max_seconds configuration of the pool,\nso you will want to set those carefully.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#disconnect_all/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.exists?/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.exists?/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#exists?/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.explain/3","doc":"Executes an EXPLAIN statement or similar for the given query according to its kind and the\nadapter in the given repository.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#explain/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.explain/3","doc":"# Postgres\n    iex> MyRepo.explain(:all, Post)\n    \"Seq Scan on posts p0  (cost=0.00..12.12 rows=1 width=443)\"\n\n    iex> Ecto.Adapters.SQL.explain(Repo, :all, Post)\n    \"Seq Scan on posts p0  (cost=0.00..12.12 rows=1 width=443)\"\n\n    # MySQL\n    iex> MyRepo.explain(:all, from(p in Post, where: p.title == \"title\")) |> IO.puts()\n    +----+-------------+-------+------------+------+---------------+------+---------+------+------+----------+-------------+\n    | id | select_type | table | partitions | type | possible_keys | key  | key_len | ref  | rows | filtered | Extra       |\n    +----+-------------+-------+------------+------+---------------+------+---------+------+------+----------+-------------+\n    |  1 | SIMPLE      | p0    | NULL       | ALL  | NULL          | NULL | NULL    | NULL |    1 |    100.0 | Using where |\n    +----+-------------+-------+------------+------+---------------+------+---------+------+------+----------+-------------+\n\n    # Shared opts\n    iex> MyRepo.explain(:all, Post, analyze: true, timeout: 20_000)\n    \"Seq Scan on posts p0  (cost=0.00..11.70 rows=170 width=443) (actual time=0.013..0.013 rows=0 loops=1)\\nPlanning Time: 0.031 ms\\nExecution Time: 0.021 ms\"\n\nIt's safe to execute it for updates and deletes, no data change will be committed:\n\n    iex> MyRepo.explain(Repo, :update_all, from(p in Post, update: [set: [title: \"new title\"]]))\n    \"Update on posts p0  (cost=0.00..11.70 rows=170 width=449)\\n  ->  Seq Scan on posts p0  (cost=0.00..11.70 rows=170 width=449)\"\n\nThis function is also available under the repository with name `explain`:\n\n    iex> MyRepo.explain(:all, from(p in Post, where: p.title == \"title\"))\n    \"Seq Scan on posts p0  (cost=0.00..12.12 rows=1 width=443)\\n  Filter: ((title)::text = 'title'::text)\"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#explain/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.explain/3","doc":"Built-in adapters support passing `opts` to the EXPLAIN statement according to the following:\n\nAdapter          | Supported opts\n---------------- | --------------\nPostgrex         | `analyze`, `verbose`, `costs`, `settings`, `buffers`, `timing`, `summary`, `format`, `plan`, `wrap_in_transaction`\nMyXQL            | `format`, `wrap_in_transaction`\n\nAll options except `format` are boolean valued and default to `false`.\n\nThe allowed `format` values are `:map`, `:yaml`, and `:text`:\n  * `:map` is the deserialized JSON encoding.\n  * `:yaml` and `:text` return the result as a string.\n\nThe built-in adapters support the following formats:\n  * Postgrex: `:map`, `:yaml` and `:text`\n  * MyXQL: `:map` and `:text`\n\nThe `wrap_in_transaction` option is a boolean that controls whether the command is run inside of a\ntransaction that is rolled back. This is useful when, for example, you'd like to use `analyze: true`\non an update or delete query without modifying data. Defaults to `true`.\n\nThe `:plan` option in Postgrex can take the values `:custom` or `:fallback_generic`. When `:custom`\nis specified, the explain plan generated will consider the specific values of the query parameters\nthat are supplied. When using `:fallback_generic`, the specific values of the query parameters will\nbe ignored. `:fallback_generic` does not use PostgreSQL's built-in support for a generic explain\nplan (available as of PostgreSQL 16), but instead uses a special implementation that works for PostgreSQL\nversions 12 and above. Defaults to `:custom`.\n\nAny other value passed to `opts` will be forwarded to the underlying adapter query function, including\nshared Repo options such as `:timeout`. Non built-in adapters may have specific behaviour and you should\nconsult their documentation for more details.\n\nFor version compatibility, please check your database's documentation:\n\n  * _Postgrex_: [PostgreSQL doc](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-explain.html).\n  * _MyXQL_: [MySQL doc](https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.0/en/explain.html).","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#explain/3-options"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.get/3","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.get/3 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#get/3"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.get!/3","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.get!/3 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#get!/3"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.get_by/3","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.get_by/3 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#get_by/3"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.get_by!/3","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.get_by!/3 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#get_by!/3"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.get_dynamic_repo/0","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.get_dynamic_repo/0 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#get_dynamic_repo/0"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.in_transaction?/0","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.in_transaction?/0 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#in_transaction?/0"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.init/2","doc":"Dynamically loads the repository url from the DATABASE_URL environment variable.\n\nThis allows migrations and runtime configuration without hardcoding database credentials.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#init/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.insert/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.insert/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#insert/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.insert!/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.insert!/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#insert!/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.insert_all/3","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.insert_all/3 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#insert_all/3"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.insert_or_update/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.insert_or_update/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#insert_or_update/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.insert_or_update!/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.insert_or_update!/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#insert_or_update!/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.load/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.load/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#load/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.migrate_up/1","doc":"Runs all pending migrations in the given direction.\n\nUsed for database setup and schema updates.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#migrate_up/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.migrate_up/1","doc":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.migrate_up()\n    BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.migrate_up(:down)","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#migrate_up/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.one/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.one/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#one/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.one!/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.one!/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#one!/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.preload/3","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.preload/3 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#preload/3"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.prepare_query/3","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.prepare_query/3 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#prepare_query/3"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.prepare_transaction/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.prepare_transaction/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#prepare_transaction/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.put_dynamic_repo/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.put_dynamic_repo/1 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#put_dynamic_repo/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.query/3","doc":"Runs a custom SQL query.\n\nIf the query was successful, it will return an `:ok` tuple containing\na map with at least two keys:\n\n  * `:num_rows` - the number of rows affected\n  * `:rows` - the result set as a list. `nil` may be returned\n    instead of the list if the command does not yield any row\n    as result (but still yields the number of affected rows,\n    like a `delete` command without returning would)","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#query/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.query/3","doc":"* `:log` - When false, does not log the query\n  * `:timeout` - Execute request timeout, accepts: `:infinity` (default: `15000`);","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#query/3-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.query/3","doc":"iex> MyRepo.query(\"SELECT $1::integer + $2\", [40, 2])\n    {:ok, %{rows: [[42]], num_rows: 1}}\n\n    iex> Ecto.Adapters.SQL.query(MyRepo, \"SELECT $1::integer + $2\", [40, 2])\n    {:ok, %{rows: [[42]], num_rows: 1}}","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#query/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.query!/3","doc":"Same as `query/3` but returns result directly without `:ok` tuple\nand raises on invalid queries","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#query!/3"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.query_many/3","doc":"Runs a custom SQL query that returns multiple results on the given repo.\n\nIn case of success, it must return an `:ok` tuple containing a list of\nmaps with at least two keys:\n\n  * `:num_rows` - the number of rows affected\n\n  * `:rows` - the result set as a list. `nil` may be returned\n    instead of the list if the command does not yield any row\n    as result (but still yields the number of affected rows,\n    like a `delete` command without returning would)","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#query_many/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.query_many/3","doc":"* `:log` - When false, does not log the query\n  * `:timeout` - Execute request timeout, accepts: `:infinity` (default: `15000`);","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#query_many/3-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.query_many/3","doc":"iex> MyRepo.query_many(\"SELECT $1; SELECT $2;\", [40, 2])\n    {:ok, [%{rows: [[40]], num_rows: 1}, %{rows: [[2]], num_rows: 1}]}\n\n    iex> Ecto.Adapters.SQL.query_many(MyRepo, \"SELECT $1; SELECT $2;\", [40, 2])\n    {:ok, [%{rows: [[40]], num_rows: 1}, %{rows: [[2]], num_rows: 1}]}","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#query_many/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.query_many!/3","doc":"Same as `query_many/4` but returns result directly without `:ok` tuple\nand raises on invalid queries","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#query_many!/3"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.reload/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.reload/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#reload/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.reload!/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.reload!/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#reload!/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.rollback/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.rollback/1 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#rollback/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.start_link/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.start_link/1 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.stop/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.stop/1 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#stop/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.stream/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.stream/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#stream/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.to_sql/2","doc":"Converts the given query to SQL according to its kind and the\nadapter in the given repository.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#to_sql/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.to_sql/2","doc":"The examples below are meant for reference. Each adapter will\nreturn a different result:\n\n    iex> MyRepo.to_sql(:all, Post)\n    {\"SELECT p.id, p.title, p.inserted_at, p.created_at FROM posts as p\", []}\n\n    iex> MyRepo.to_sql(:update_all, from(p in Post, update: [set: [title: ^\"hello\"]]))\n    {\"UPDATE posts AS p SET title = $1\", [\"hello\"]}\n\n    iex> Ecto.Adapters.SQL.to_sql(:all, MyRepo, Post)\n    {\"SELECT p.id, p.title, p.inserted_at, p.created_at FROM posts as p\", []}","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#to_sql/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.transact/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.transact/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#transact/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.transaction/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.transaction/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#transaction/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.update/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.update/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#update/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.update!/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.update!/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#update!/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.update_all/3","doc":"Callback implementation for  Ecto.Repo.update_all/3 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Ecto.Repo.html#update_all/3"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Monitor","doc":"Monitors bot heartbeats and publishes alerts when bots go stale.\n\nSubscribes to `bot.army.health.>` on NATS, tracks last-seen timestamps\nin ETS, and checks every 30s for entries older than 60s. Stale bots\nget an alert published to `bot.army.health.stale`; recovery events\ngo to `bot.army.health.recovered`.\n\nPublic ETS reads via `get_status/1`, `list_bots/0`, `list_stale/0`\ndon't require GenServer calls.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Monitor.html"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Monitor.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Monitor.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Monitor.get_status/1","doc":"Returns `{:ok, {last_seen_at, status}}` or `:unknown`.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Monitor.html#get_status/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Monitor.list_bots/0","doc":"Lists all tracked bots as `[{bot_id, last_seen_at, status}]`.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Monitor.html#list_bots/0"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Monitor.list_stale/0","doc":"Lists stale bots as `[{bot_id, last_seen_at, stale_for_sec}]`.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Monitor.html#list_stale/0"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Monitor.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Monitor.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Responder","doc":"Shared health check responder for Bot Army services.\n\nSubscribes to `bot. .health` on NATS (request/reply pattern).\nReports NATS connectivity, database connectivity, key process liveness, and version.\n\nRe-registers with ConnectionRegistry on reconnect so the health subscription\nis always active.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Responder.html"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Responder.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Responder.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Responder.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Health.Responder.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Logging","doc":"Helper for any bot to record structured activity entries to the GTD daily log.\n\nThis module provides a simple interface for bots to publish log entries without\nknowing about GTD internals. Entries are published to `gtd.log.create` where\nthe GTD bot processes them.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Logging.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage - BotArmyRuntime.Logging","doc":"```elixir\nBotArmyRuntime.Logging.record(\"Task completed successfully\", source: \"advocacy_bot\")\nBotArmyRuntime.Logging.record(\"New bill found\", source: \"advocacy_bot\", category: \"work\", tags: [\"bill\", \"federal\"])\n```","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Logging.html#module-usage"},{"type":"module","title":"Options - BotArmyRuntime.Logging","doc":"- `source` (required) - Bot or component name (e.g., \"advocacy_bot\", \"liveview\")\n- `category` - One of: work, personal, health, learning, care, admin, social (default: \"personal\")\n- `task_id` - Optional link to a GTD task ID\n- `tags` - List of string tags for categorization","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Logging.html#module-options"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Logging.record/2","doc":"Record a log entry.\n\nThe `body` is required and should be a brief description of what occurred.\n\nReturns `:ok` or `{:error, reason}`.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Logging.html#record/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - BotArmyRuntime.Logging.record/2","doc":"- `source` - Bot or component name (required)\n- `category` - work | personal | health | learning | care | admin | social\n- `task_id` - Link to a task ID\n- `tags` - List of string tags","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Logging.html#record/2-options"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Metrics.Endpoint","doc":"HTTP endpoint serving Prometheus metrics at /metrics on port 9090.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Metrics.Endpoint.html"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Metrics.Endpoint.call/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Plug.call/2 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Metrics.Endpoint.html#call/2"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Metrics.Endpoint.init/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  Plug.init/1 .","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Metrics.Endpoint.html#init/1"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Metrics.PromExPlugin","doc":"Custom PromEx plugin for Bot Army NATS and connection metrics.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Metrics.PromExPlugin.html"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection","doc":"Manages the connection to the NATS message bus.\n\nResponsibilities:\n- Establishing and maintaining a connection to NATS\n- Handling reconnection with exponential backoff\n- Managing the connection state\n- Providing a connection handle for publishers","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Configuration - BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection","doc":"Configure in `config.exs`:\n\n    config :bot_army_runtime, :nats,\n      servers: [{\"localhost\", 4222}],\n      ping_interval: 30_000,\n      max_reconnect_attempts: 10,\n      reconnect_delay_ms: 1000","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"module","title":"Connection Handle - BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection","doc":"The connection is stored in a named GenServer under `:gnat` key.\nPublishers access it via `GenServer.call(BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection, :get_connection)`.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection.html#module-connection-handle"},{"type":"module","title":"Error Handling - BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection","doc":"Connection failures are logged and recovery is attempted automatically.\nIf max reconnect attempts are exceeded, the application is halted.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection.html#module-error-handling"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection.subscribe_to_status/0","doc":"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection.html#subscribe_to_status/0"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection.unsubscribe_from_status/0","doc":"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection.html#unsubscribe_from_status/0"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Dedup","doc":"ETS-based sliding window deduplication for NATS events.\n\nPrevents duplicate processing of messages that may be redelivered\nby JetStream or retried by publishers. Uses a 1-minute sliding\nwindow with up to 10K entries.\n\nFast read path via ETS — no GenServer call needed for `seen?/1`.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Dedup.html"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Dedup.check_and_mark/1","doc":"Check and mark atomically. Returns `:new` if not seen, `:duplicate` if already seen.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Dedup.html#check_and_mark/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Dedup.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Dedup.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Dedup.mark_seen/1","doc":"Mark an event_id as seen. Fast ETS insert.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Dedup.html#mark_seen/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Dedup.seen?/1","doc":"Check if an event_id has been seen within the dedup window.\nFast ETS lookup — no GenServer call.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Dedup.html#seen?/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Dedup.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Dedup.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream","doc":"JetStream stream and consumer management for Bot Army services.\n\nProvides idempotent creation of streams and durable consumers,\nensuring messages are not lost during consumer disconnects.\n\nUses the gnat Jetstream API (Gnat.Jetstream.API.Stream and\nGnat.Jetstream.API.Consumer for creation, Gnat.Jetstream for ack/nack).","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Stream Topology - BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream","doc":"| Stream | Subjects | Retention |\n|--------|----------|----------|\n| BOT_GTD | gtd.> | 30 days |\n| BOT_LLM | llm.> | 7 days |\n| BOT_JOBS | job.> | 30 days |\n| BOT_EVENTS | events.> | 30 days |\n| BOT_CLAUDE | bot_army.claude.> | 7 days |\n| BOT_FITNESS | fitness.> | 7 days |\n| BOT_CHORE | chore.> | 7 days |\n| BOT_SRE | sre.> | 7 days |\n| BOT_DLQ | dlq.> | 30 days |","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream.html#module-stream-topology"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream.ack/1","doc":"Acknowledge a JetStream message (confirm successful processing).","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream.html#ack/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream.ensure_all_streams/1","doc":"Ensure all Bot Army streams exist. Idempotent — safe to call on every startup.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream.html#ensure_all_streams/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream.ensure_consumer/4","doc":"Ensure a durable JetStream consumer exists. Idempotent.\n\nOptions:\n- `:deliver_subject` — push delivery subject (required for push consumers)\n- `:deliver_policy` — `:last` (default), `:all`, `:new`\n- `:max_deliver` — max redelivery attempts (default 3)\n- `:ack_policy` — `:explicit` (default), `:all`, `:none`\n- `:ack_wait` — ack timeout in nanoseconds (default 30s)","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream.html#ensure_consumer/4"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream.ensure_stream/4","doc":"Ensure a JetStream stream exists. Idempotent — no-op if stream already exists.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream.html#ensure_stream/4"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream.nack/1","doc":"Negatively acknowledge a JetStream message (trigger redelivery).","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream.html#nack/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream.stream_configs/0","doc":"Return the stream configurations for external use (e.g., Salt automation).","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.JetStream.html#stream_configs/0"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher","doc":"Publishes messages to NATS.\n\nHandles JSON serialization, error handling, and logging for all message publishing.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage - BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher","doc":"{:ok, _} = BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.publish(\"bot.task.created\", event_data)","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.html#module-usage"},{"type":"module","title":"Configuration - BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher","doc":"Uses NATS configuration from `:bot_army_runtime, :nats` (same as `BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Connection`).","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"module","title":"Error Handling - BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher","doc":"Returns `{:ok, subject}` on success or `{:error, reason}` on failure.\nLogs all publishing attempts for debugging.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.html#module-error-handling"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.publish/3","doc":"Publishes a message to a NATS subject.\n\nThe payload is JSON-encoded and published with the NATS envelope structure.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.html#publish/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.publish/3","doc":"- `subject` - NATS subject as a string, e.g., \"bot.task.created\"\n  - `payload` - Map or any JSON-serializable data\n  - `opts` - Optional keyword list with:\n    - `:reply_to` - Subject to expect a reply on (optional)\n    - `:timeout_ms` - Timeout for the operation (default: 5000)","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.html#publish/3-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.publish/3","doc":"- `{:ok, subject}` - Message published successfully\n  - `{:error, reason}` - Publishing failed with reason","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.html#publish/3-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.publish/3","doc":"{:ok, \"bot.task.created\"} = Publisher.publish(\"bot.task.created\", %{\"task_id\" => 123})\n\n    {:ok, _} = Publisher.publish(\"bot.task.updated\", data, reply_to: \"my.reply.subject\")","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.html#publish/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.request/3","doc":"Publishes a message and waits for a reply (request-reply pattern).\n\nUseful for synchronous operations that expect a response from a service.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.html#request/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.request/3","doc":"- `subject` - NATS subject to publish to\n  - `payload` - Message payload\n  - `timeout_ms` - Time to wait for a reply (default: 5000)","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.html#request/3-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.request/3","doc":"- `{:ok, reply_payload}` - Reply received (decoded as map)\n  - `{:error, :timeout}` - No reply received within timeout\n  - `{:error, reason}` - Publishing or connection failed","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.NATS.Publisher.html#request/3-returns"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter","doc":"Message formatter with bot personality symbols.\n\nPrepends a bot's symbol to outbound messages for consistent visual identity across all surfaces.\nThe symbol is always preserved regardless of surface constraints.\n\nReference: `/docs/north_star_docs/BOT_ARMY_PERSONALITY_NORTH_STAR.md`","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter.html"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter.symbol/1","doc":"Get just the symbol for a bot (useful for surfaces with extreme character constraints).","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter.html#symbol/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter.symbol/1","doc":"iex> BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter.symbol(:gtd_bot)\n    \"◉\"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter.html#symbol/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter.with_symbol/2","doc":"Format a message with the bot's symbol.\n\nThe symbol is always prepended, making the bot instantly recognizable\nacross all surfaces (G2 glasses, Watch, LiveView, Terminal, etc).","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter.html#with_symbol/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter.with_symbol/2","doc":"- `bot_name` - Atom identifying the bot (e.g., :gtd_bot, :fitness_bot)\n- `message` - String message to format","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter.html#with_symbol/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter.with_symbol/2","doc":"iex> BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter.with_symbol(:gtd_bot, \"Inbox cleared\")\n    \"◉ Inbox cleared\"\n\n    iex> BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter.with_symbol(:fitness_bot, \"4-day streak\")\n    \"▲ 4-day streak\"\n\nReturns the message with symbol prepended, or the original message if the bot is not registered.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Formatter.html#with_symbol/2-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity","doc":"Bot Army personality symbols registry.\n\nEach bot has a single Unicode symbol for instant recognition across all surfaces.\nSymbols are the one non-negotiable identity element — preserved regardless of surface constraints.\n\nReference: `/docs/north_star_docs/BOT_ARMY_PERSONALITY_NORTH_STAR.md`","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.html"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.all_bots/0","doc":"Get all bots as a map.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.html#all_bots/0"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.name/1","doc":"Get the name for a given bot.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.html#name/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.name/1","doc":"iex> BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.name(:gtd_bot)\n    \"Morgan\"\n\n    iex> BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.name(:trading_bot)\n    nil","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.html#name/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.registered?/1","doc":"Check if a bot has a registered symbol.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.html#registered?/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.symbol/1","doc":"Get the symbol for a given bot.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.html#symbol/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.symbol/1","doc":"iex> BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.symbol(:gtd_bot)\n    \"◉\"\n\n    iex> BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.symbol(:fitness_bot)\n    \"▲\"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Personality.Identity.html#symbol/1-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.PromEx","doc":"PromEx module for Bot Army metrics collection.\n\nCollects NATS, BEAM, and Ecto metrics via PromEx plugins.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.PromEx.html"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.PromEx.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.PromEx.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry","doc":"Sets up telemetry handlers for observability across Bot Army services.\n\nHandles:\n- Ecto query metrics\n- NATS publishing metrics\n- Application-level logging\n- Error tracking via Sentry (when configured)","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry.html"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry.handle_ecto_error/4","doc":"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry.html#handle_ecto_error/4"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry.handle_ecto_query/4","doc":"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry.html#handle_ecto_query/4"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry.handle_nats_error/4","doc":"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry.html#handle_nats_error/4"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry.handle_nats_publish/4","doc":"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry.html#handle_nats_publish/4"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Telemetry.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant","doc":"Tenant management utilities for multi-tenancy support.\n\nThis module provides utilities for working with tenants in the Bot Army\necosystem, including the default tenant ID and tenant-aware subject routing.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Default Tenant - BotArmyRuntime.Tenant","doc":"Abby's personal deployment uses `tenant_id = \"default\"`. This is the\nsingle-tenant case that existing bots handle.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.html#module-default-tenant"},{"type":"module","title":"Subject Prefixing - BotArmyRuntime.Tenant","doc":"Tenant-specific NATS subjects follow the pattern:\n    tenant. .events.*\n    tenant. .gtd.*\n    etc.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.html#module-subject-prefixing"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage - BotArmyRuntime.Tenant","doc":"# Get the default tenant ID\n    BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.default_tenant_id()\n\n    # Build a tenant-aware subject\n    subject = BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.subject(\"gtd.task.list\", \"default\")\n\n    # Extract tenant from a subject\n    tenant_id = BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.from_subject(\"tenant.abc123.gtd.tasks\")","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.html#module-usage"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.default_tenant_id/0","doc":"Returns the default tenant UUID for single-tenant deployments.\n\nAbby's personal deployment uses `\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001\"` as the tenant ID.\nSaaS tenants will have unique UUIDs assigned at provisioning.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.html#default_tenant_id/0"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.from_subject/1","doc":"Extracts tenant ID from a tenant-prefixed subject.\n\nReturns `nil` if the subject doesn't match the tenant prefix pattern.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.html#from_subject/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.from_subject/1","doc":"iex> BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.from_subject(\"tenant.default.gtd.tasks\")\n    \"default\"\n\n    iex> BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.from_subject(\"gtd.tasks\")\n    nil","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.html#from_subject/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.strip_tenant_prefix/1","doc":"Strips the tenant prefix from a subject, returning the core subject.\n\nReturns `nil` if the subject is not tenant-prefixed.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.html#strip_tenant_prefix/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.strip_tenant_prefix/1","doc":"iex> BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.strip_tenant_prefix(\"tenant.00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001.gtd.tasks\")\n    \"gtd.tasks\"\n\n    iex> BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.strip_tenant_prefix(\"gtd.tasks\")\n    nil","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.html#strip_tenant_prefix/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.subject/2","doc":"Builds a tenant-prefixed NATS subject.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.html#subject/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.subject/2","doc":"iex> BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.subject(\"gtd.task.list\", \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001\")\n    \"tenant.00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001.gtd.task.list\"\n\n    iex> BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.subject(\"dungeon.session.start\", \"acme-corp\")\n    \"tenant.acme-corp.dungeon.session.start\"","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.html#subject/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.tenant_subject?/1","doc":"Checks if a subject is tenant-prefixed.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.html#tenant_subject?/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.tenant_subject?/1","doc":"iex> BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.tenant_subject?(\"tenant.00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001.gtd.tasks\")\n    true\n\n    iex> BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.tenant_subject?(\"gtd.tasks\")\n    false","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tenant.html#tenant_subject?/1-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing","doc":"OpenTelemetry distributed tracing integration for NATS message flows.\n\nProvides helpers for:\n- Injecting trace context into outgoing NATS messages (publisher side)\n- Extracting trace context from incoming NATS messages (consumer side)\n- Creating spans around NATS publish and consume operations","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Configuration - BotArmyRuntime.Tracing","doc":"Set `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` env var (e.g., `http://localhost:4318`)\nto enable trace export. If unset, the noop exporter is used.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage (Publisher) - BotArmyRuntime.Tracing","doc":"headers = BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.inject_trace_context([])\n    Gnat.pub(conn, subject, payload, headers: headers)","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.html#module-usage-publisher"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage (Consumer) - BotArmyRuntime.Tracing","doc":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.with_consumer_span(msg.topic, Map.get(msg, :headers), fn ->\n      # process message\n    end)","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.html#module-usage-consumer"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.add_trace_context_to_envelope/1","doc":"Adds trace context to a NATS envelope payload map.\n\nInjects a `_trace_context` field containing the current `traceparent`\nstring. This is a secondary propagation mechanism for systems that\nread envelope bodies rather than NATS headers.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.html#add_trace_context_to_envelope/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.configured?/0","doc":"Returns whether OpenTelemetry is configured with a real exporter.\n\nUseful for conditionally enabling tracing overhead only when a backend\nis available.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.html#configured?/0"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.extract_trace_context/1","doc":"Extracts W3C trace context from NATS message headers.\n\nSets the extracted context in the process dictionary so subsequent\n`start_span` calls become children of the extracted trace.\n\nReturns `:ok` regardless — extraction is best-effort.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.html#extract_trace_context/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.extract_trace_context_from_envelope/1","doc":"Extracts trace context from a NATS envelope payload map.\n\nReads `_trace_context.traceparent` from the envelope body and sets\nthe process context so subsequent spans link correctly.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.html#extract_trace_context_from_envelope/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.inject_trace_context/1","doc":"Injects W3C trace context into a list of NATS headers.\n\nReturns a new headers list with `traceparent` and `tracestate` added\nif there's an active span. If no span is active, returns headers unchanged.\n\nNATS headers are `[{key, value}]` tuples.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.html#inject_trace_context/1"},{"type":"function","title":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.with_consumer_span/3","doc":"Wraps a function in a consumer span, extracting trace context from headers.\n\nCreates a child span linked to the parent trace (if present in headers),\nexecutes the function, and ends the span. Records exceptions as span events.","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.html#with_consumer_span/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.with_consumer_span/3","doc":"- `subject` - NATS subject the message arrived on\n  - `headers` - NATS message headers (list of `{key, value}` tuples)\n  - `fun` - 0-arity function to execute within the span","ref":"BotArmyRuntime.Tracing.html#with_consumer_span/3-arguments"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.40.1"}}